---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Nickel 200 / 201" active="/products">
  <section class="pagebanner">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--blue)">Commercially Pure Nickel</p>
      <h1>Nickel 200 / 201</h1>
      <p>Solid-solution-strengthened, commercially pure wrought nickel with excellent resistance to corrosives — in particular hydroxides.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="visual">
    <img src="/product-nickel.webp" alt="Nickel 200 and 201 product photography" />
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell productcontent">
      <aside>Bhansali Metals<br />Product briefing</aside>
      <div>
<h3>Nickel (200 & 201)</h3>
<p>Nickel 200 and Nickel 201 are solid-solution-strengthened, commercially pure wrought materials with good mechanical properties over a wide range of temperatures and excellent resistance to many corrosives, in particular hydroxides. Nickel 201 is a modification of 200 controlling carbon (0.02 max), which keeps it from embrittlement by intergranular precipitates at 600°F to 1400°F in many processes. Typically the elemental restrictions of both are combined into one dual-certified chemistry — a single alloy with the desired characteristics of both: Nickel 200/201.</p>
<h3>Forms stocked at Bhansali Metals</h3>
        <div class="details">
        <div>
          <b>Sheet</b>
          <span>Commercially pure nickel sheet for caustic, food and electronics duty</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <b>Plate</b>
          <span>Heavy-gauge plate for fabricated process equipment</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <b>Bar</b>
          <span>Round, square and hex bar 3–150 mm</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <b>Pipe & tube</b>
          <span>Welded and seamless pipe and tube</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <b>Fittings</b>
          <span>Flanges, slip-ons, blinds, weld-necks, lap joints, long welding necks, socket welds, elbows, tees, stub-ends, returns, caps, crosses, reducers and pipe nipples</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <b>Wire</b>
          <span>Drawn wire 0.6–8 mm</span>
        </div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top:2rem">
          <a class="button" href="/enquiry">Request a quote <svg class="ic" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"/><path d="M7 17 17 7"/></svg></a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
